{"parentUuid":"f92d3704-6a9d-4bc5-b462-e609dab280b6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"30303ae5-8077-446b-84bf-dc8ec96db362","agentId":"ac07b073c0dacf54f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014Lct7rPnmvMGDw4Q1ezLfq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{# MES handoff cards -- 2026-10-14 pass.\n2\t\n3\t   Included once per page (not once per row): ``tests.html`` sets\n4\t   ``mes_handoff_vin = view.vin`` before including this; ``job.html``'s\n5\t   step 6 section sets ``mes_handoff_vin = vin``. Everything else is\n6\t   client-side -- this fetches the small MES-function catalogue once\n7\t   (GET /api/tests/mes-handoff/candidates), matches it against whatever\n8\t   test rows (``.ts-row[id^=\"test-\"]``) or job checklist steps\n9\t   (``.checklist-step[id^=\"fb-\"]``) are already on the page, and injects a\n10\t   card right after each match. Nothing here writes to the car -- the\n11\t   \"Import the MES log\" button only reads a file MES already wrote\n12\t   (POST /api/tests/{vin}/mes-import) and records it in this feature's own\n13\t   ledger; the pass/fail buttons and done/outcome checkbox each row already\n14\t   has are the only result-recording controls on either page. #}\n15\t<div id=\"mes-handoff-root\" data-vin=\"{{ mes_handoff_vin or '' }}\" hidden></div>\n16\t<template id=\"mes-handoff-card-tpl\">"}]},"uuid":"710e12b1-a3ae-4d88-aa64-b8d2e5ea6ed4","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:16:13.003Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\web\\templates\\_mes_handoff.html","content":"{# MES handoff cards -- 2026-10-14 pass.\n\n   Included once per page (not once per row): ``tests.html`` sets\n   ``mes_handoff_vin = view.vin`` before including this; ``job.html``'s\n   step 6 section sets ``mes_handoff_vin = vin``. Everything else is\n   client-side -- this fetches the small MES-function catalogue once\n   (GET /api/tests/mes-handoff/candidates), matches it against whatever\n   test rows (``.ts-row[id^=\"test-\"]``) or job checklist steps\n   (``.checklist-step[id^=\"fb-\"]``) are already on the page, and injects a\n   card right after each match. Nothing here writes to the car -- the\n   \"Import the MES log\" button only reads a file MES already wrote\n   (POST /api/tests/{vin}/mes-import) and records it in this feature's own\n   ledger; the pass/fail buttons and done/outcome checkbox each row already\n   has are the only result-recording controls on either page. #}\n<div id=\"mes-handoff-root\" data-vin=\"{{ mes_handoff_vin or '' }}\" hidden></div>\n<template id=\"mes-handoff-card-tpl\">","numLines":16,"startLine":1,"totalLines":140}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f92d3704-6a9d-4bc5-b462-e609dab280b6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
