{"parentUuid":"95a4f6e3-bc9b-456a-8719-0d1a17cafa55","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ac07b073c0dacf54f","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg23bNiEyDYSJ1zrS9ixK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GUKYMFHkizwRkjbeZk831S","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"Committed and pushed to github/main: commit 545abb8fafe1c5208d8cbbba240dc3c6b62e4007\n\"MES vs CUORE capability matrix; MES handoff cards; MES logs get the same scan entry and health report\"\n\nFiles added/changed (only my owned files; nothing else in the dirty tree was touched or staged):\n- docs/research/MES_VS_CUORE_CAPABILITY_2026-10-14.md (new) — the matrix doc, generated from mes_functions.py so the two can't drift. Research: multiecuscan.net's supported-vehicle page + forum, giuliaforums/stelvioforum/giuliatech/alfaowner/mhhauto writeups, and a read-only pass over the local install's Lang\\English.txt UI string table (CONFIRMED-tier source for coil/idle actuator and key/RF learning rows) and its FES logs. Covers where MES is better (TCM/BCM/ABS parameter scaling, adjustments, coding, cable guidance, IHS/CH reach) and where CUORE is better (verdict/evidence gate, Mode 06, cross-session history, hypotheses, mobile, honesty labels) — plus one deliberately honest exception: epb_service_mode, where owner reports say MES's own menu doesn't work and the car's native infotainment does the job instead.\n- mes-log-mcp/mes/mes_functions.py (new) — 31 functions (≥25 required), every one sourced, none invented; public reads: all_functions/function/functions_for_module/functions_for_test/search.\n- cuore/services/mes_handoff_bridge.py (new) — handoff-card lookup (candidates/find_for_test/find_for_text/card) and MES log import (import_mes_log/list_mes_scans/health_line). Import keeps its own small ledger (mes_imports.json) tagged source.kind=\"MES\" rather than disguising an MES-captured file as a live serial read — calls mes.scan_health.verdict() (that module's own public function) for the health line, never edits scanlog/scan_health files.\n- cuore/web/templates/_mes_handoff.html (new) — one client-side script, included once each from tests.html and job.html step 6, fetches the small function catalogue once and injects a card after matching test rows / checklist steps; adds an \"Import the MES log\" action when relevant. Never adds a second result-recording control — reuses the existing PASS/FAIL buttons (tests.html) and done/outcome checkbox (job.html step 6).\n- cuore/web/templates/tests.html, job.html — one include line each (additive, confirmed via git diff).\n- cuore/api/tests.py — additive routes only: GET /tests/mes-handoff/candidates, /by-test/{id}, /by-text; POST /tests/{vin}/mes-import; GET /tests/{vin}/mes-scans.\n- cuore/tests/check_mes_handoff.py (new) — 38 checks, all passing.\n\nTest results: check_mes_handoff.py 38/38, check_tests_page.py 85/85, check_jobs_page.py 24/24, check_screens.py 28/28 — all green, no regressions.\n\nNote: the working tree has substantial unrelated dirty/untracked files from other concurrent work (experience_*, system_detail_bridge, poller/stream/transport/uds, koch-mcp/, etc.) — none of those were staged, edited, or committed.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":212,"cache_read_input_tokens":243751,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":212,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01GUKYMFHkizwRkjbeZk831S":{"message":"Committed and pushed to github/main: commit 545abb8fafe1c5208d8cbbba240dc3c6b62e4007\n\"MES vs CUORE capability matrix; MES handoff cards; MES logs get the same scan entry and health report\"\n\nFiles added/changed (only my owned files; nothing else in the dirty tree was touched or staged):\n- docs/research/MES_VS_CUORE_CAPABILITY_2026-10-14.md (new) — the matrix doc, generated from mes_functions.py so the two can't drift. Research: multiecuscan.net's supported-vehicle page + forum, giuliaforums/stelvioforum/giuliatech/alfaowner/mhhauto writeups, and a read-only pass over the local install's Lang\\English.txt UI string table (CONFIRMED-tier source for coil/idle actuator and key/RF learning rows) and its FES logs. Covers where MES is better (TCM/BCM/ABS parameter scaling, adjustments, coding, cable guidance, IHS/CH reach) and where CUORE is better (verdict/evidence gate, Mode 06, cross-session history, hypotheses, mobile, honesty labels) — plus one deliberately honest exception: epb_service_mode, where owner reports say MES's own menu doesn't work and the car's native infotainment does the job instead.\n- mes-log-mcp/mes/mes_functions.py (new) — 31 functions (≥25 required), every one sourced, none invented; public reads: all_functions/function/functions_for_module/functions_for_test/search.\n- cuore/services/mes_handoff_bridge.py (new) — handoff-card lookup (candidates/find_for_test/find_for_text/card) and MES log import (import_mes_log/list_mes_scans/health_line). Import keeps its own small ledger (mes_imports.json) tagged source.kind=\"MES\" rather than disguising an MES-captured file as a live serial read — calls mes.scan_health.verdict() (that module's own public function) for the health line, never edits scanlog/scan_health files.\n- cuore/web/templates/_mes_handoff.html (new) — one client-side script, included once each from tests.html and job.html step 6, fetches the small function catalogue once and injects a card after matching test rows / checklist steps; adds an \"Import the MES log\" action when relevant. Never adds a second result-recording control — reuses the existing PASS/FAIL buttons (tests.html) and done/outcome checkbox (job.html step 6).\n- cuore/web/templates/tests.html, job.html — one include line each (additive, confirmed via git diff).\n- cuore/api/tests.py — additive routes only: GET /tests/mes-handoff/candidates, /by-test/{id}, /by-text; POST /tests/{vin}/mes-import; GET /tests/{vin}/mes-scans.\n- cuore/tests/check_mes_handoff.py (new) — 38 checks, all passing.\n\nTest results: check_mes_handoff.py 38/38, check_tests_page.py 85/85, check_jobs_page.py 24/24, check_screens.py 28/28 — all green, no regressions.\n\nNote: the working tree has substantial unrelated dirty/untracked files from other concurrent work (experience_*, system_detail_bridge, poller/stream/transport/uds, koch-mcp/, etc.) — none of those were staged, edited, or committed.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"9d9ed496-fa49-489b-bc3e-694d3730f7fa","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cg23bNQe1gegZBVnWqzq8","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"d183f343-014e-4a2f-a602-ca917428889e","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:24:43.747Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
